    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "JON",
      "chapter": 4,
      "chapter_usfm": "JON.4",
      "version_id": 3034,
      "version_abbr": "BSB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "JON.4.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Jonah, however, was greatly displeased, and he became angry."
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "JON.4.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "So he prayed to the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "JON.4.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "And now, O Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "JON.4.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "JON.4.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Then Jonah left the city and sat down east of it, where he made himself a shelter and sat in its shade to see what would happen to the city."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "JON.4.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "So the Lord and it grew up to provide shade over Jonah’s head to ease his discomfort, and Jonah was greatly pleased with the plant."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "JON.4.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "When dawn came the next day, God appointed a worm that attacked the plant so that it withered."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "JON.4.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "As the sun was rising, God appointed a scorching east wind, and the sun beat down on Jonah’s head so that he grew faint and wished to die, saying, “It is better for me to die than to live.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "JON.4.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Then God asked Jonah, “Have you any right to be angry about the plant?”“I do,” he replied. “I am angry enough to die!”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "JON.4.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But the Lord"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "JON.4.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "So should I not care about the great city of Nineveh, which has more than 120,000 people who cannot tell their right hand from their left, and many cattle as well?”"
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 11,
      "headings": [],
      "footnotes": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "JON.4.1",
          "note_ref": "4:1",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Or It was exceedingly evil to Jonah, and he became angry"
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "JON.4.6",
          "note_ref": "4:6",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Hebrew qiqayon; that is, possibly the castor oil plant; also in verses 7, 9, and 10"
        }
      ],
